I walk out of the fitting room with my new jacket.
The shop assistant comes over to me.
"We also have winter accessories over there," she says and points.
I look over at some small tables.
The tables are full of warm things.
I need to protect my ears and my hands against the cold.
On the first table lie many different scarves.
I touch them to feel the material.
I choose a soft scarf.
It is made of wool and is wonderfully warm.
Next to them lies a large selection of beanies.
I look at the many beautiful colors.
I try on a yellow beanie, but it itches a bit.
Then I find a red beanie instead.
It is very soft and warm on the ears.
Finally, I only need something for my hands.
My hands are always very cold here in Copenhagen.
I look at a small rack with gloves.
I quickly find a pair of thick black gloves.
Now I am ready to go out into the frost again.
